# Pinned by structural source scans (host/[slug].test.ts, [slug].test.ts): these
# files' inline scripts are asserted as literal text, so re-wrapping a line does
# not just fail a guard — it can silently disarm one. The timer guard in the host
# panel's suite went from "exactly one fetching timer" to matching nothing at
# all when Prettier reflowed the script. Formatting is not worth a guard that
# cannot fail (test-plan.md §2 Risk #2).
#
# **These paths moved with the pages** (multiple-quizzes): `host.astro` became
# `host/[slug].astro` and `index.astro` became `[slug].astro`. A stale entry here
# is silent in both directions — the suite goes red at best, and at worst a
# reflow disarms a guard on the way past. The `[` and `]` are escaped because
# `.prettierignore` reads gitignore glob syntax, where a bare `[slug]` is a
# character class matching one of `s l u g` and would not match this file.
src/pages/quiz/\[slug\].astro
src/pages/quiz/host/\[slug\].astro

# `/quiz` and `/quiz/host` are the two entry pages that replaced the addresses
# those views vacated. They carry no inline script and no source scan, so they
# are formatted normally — listed here only so a reader looking for them knows
# their absence is deliberate.
